From d5f32a6a5f65fc3f799550e1af9bf7435e3da17c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:22:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(threadmill)!: thread-mill tool kinds and a reworked
 helical thread-milling operation

Tool model: two new kinds, thread_mill (multi-form: rows of teeth at one
pitch) and thread_mill_single (single-form: one row, a pitch range), with
the new Tool field pitch_min. Sanity law, pitch door and form door in
camcraft-tools::thread_mill; library and project file round-trip; the tool
editor, the tree, the operation digest; two starter-catalog tools. The
program simulation sweeps a thread mill at its tooth roots, as it does a tap.

Thread operation: the kernel is rewritten. Radial passes are full helices
(equal steps, the last on the ISO thread depth); a single-form mill winds one
turn per thread, a multi-form mill one revolution per level; tangential lead
arcs that keep the helix's axial rate; climb / conventional and right / left
hand by the handbook rule under an M3 spindle; the tip never below the floor,
no rapid below the feature's top; the feed stated at the cutting edge and
programmed at the tool centre. The operation gains pitch (optional) and hand.
The old ride could not post at all (the crossing and tangency laws convicted
every move), cut the top threads shallower than the bottom ones, and wound a
left-hand helix under its default setting.

Gouge laws: the tooth crests are judged against the thread's major circle
(tangency), the body under the teeth against the part solid with no allowance
at the tip (solid law); the crossing law stands down for Thread only.

Refusals by name when the operation is made, edited, retyped or re-tooled and
again at generate: a pitch outside the tool's range or other than a
multi-form mill's, a form other than 60 degrees, an infeed past the thread
depth, a mill no smaller than a hole's minor diameter.

External threads are cut by the kernel (pinned, golden) but not yet offered
by the operation (#985). Still owed: the thread form in the simulation
(#986), other thread forms (#987), pass controls (#988), the MCP skill text
(#989). Decisions and sources: docs/decisions/894-thread-mill.md.

BREAKING CHANGE: a Thread operation no longer accepts a Tap-kind tool; an
existing one names its tool and refuses to generate until the tool is
re-kinded as a thread mill. Every existing Thread operation reads Stale once
and regenerates to the new ride. Tool gains the field pitch_min.

Refs #894

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
